// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/turbobaby/pricing_honesty.t27 -- an absent rate is not zero, and a dash is not silence
; The formal statement of DECISIONS.md D11 (price provenance) and D9 (absent stays absent) for
; one value: the published per-day rate of a bike family. Source of truth for the optional-rate
; representation the two runtimes named by D15 must share -- src/trios/pricing.rs for the Axum
; server and for the Dioxus/WASM catalog screen -- so that the honesty filters are written once
; and checked against a written contract instead of against each other. ASCII only (L3).

; WHY (measured 2026-09-12, data/fleet_seed.json, schema_version 2). Issue #21 opens with
; "five of thirteen families have no measured rate". THAT FIGURE IS NOT REPRODUCIBLE. Counted
; row by row: of the 14 in-stock families exactly ONE lacks base_rate_thb_day -- click-125 --
; and that row also carries offered:false with 0 of its 1 unit available, so of the 13 OFFERED
; families ZERO lack a rate. The seed's own totals agree with the row count and not with the
; issue: families_without_published_rate is 1. The issue's five is recorded below as a
; constant and refuted by a test, because a spec built around it would have pinned a defect
; that does not exist, and because the correction is the most useful thing in this file.

; The absence in this corpus is real, but it points the other way and it is seven times
; larger: price_list_only holds 7 families with a published rate and ZERO units, and they
; must never read as available. So both failure modes are live at once -- one family with
; stock and no rate, seven with a rate and no stock -- which is why presence-of-rate and
; bookability are kept as two independent facts here and neither is derived from the other.
; A third measured absence keeps that separation honest: xadv-750 is bookable (offered, 1 of
; 2 units at base) and has a present day rate of 2788, yet its monthly_low_season_thb is
; null. Absence is not confined to the closed family, so "bookable implies present" is
; claimed for the per-day rate only and is not generalised to every money field. Four money
; fields are null across the 14 in-stock rows: click-125's rate, deposit and monthly, and
; xadv-750's monthly.

; D11 is quoted rather than paraphrased, because it outranks convenience: the client-facing
; price is the number the door (the owner's live sheet) returns; if the door is silent the
; bot MUST NOT compute a price -- not an exact number, not a "from" number, not an average,
; not a range -- and not silence either. It says that a human quotes this price. Invention
; and silence are forbidden equally. That is why the dash sentinel cannot travel alone here:
; every SHAPE_DASH carries SAY_HUMAN_QUOTES, and a renderer that emits the dash without the
; sentence has committed the silence half of the offence instead of the invention half. A
; spec that shipped the dash alone would license silence, which is the same defect wearing
; better manners.

; WHAT THIS SPEC NEVER DOES. It holds no default rate, no coalescing operator and no fallback
; price. There is no function here from an absent rate to a number, and that missing function
; IS the specification -- "it compiles" would prove nothing, since a file of bare constants
; compiles too. It computes no client price at all: the class discounts (scooter 0.25,
; motorcycle 0.15) and the published term bands live in the seed, the arithmetic lives once
; in src/trios/pricing.rs (D15), and this file only pins that the handing-over cannot invent
; a number. It carries no renter, handle, phone, debt, key code, tax date, purchase cost,
; plate or personal note (D14) -- not in a constant and not in a test fixture. It does not
; distinguish a silent door from an unpublished tariff, because the client-facing consequence
; of the two is identical. It no longer disclaims the divergence rule, and that sentence is
; corrected rather than left standing: until 2026-09-20 this paragraph said "the divergence log
; D11 requires is a different contract", which was wrong about the DECISION and right only
; about the record. The decision -- the one-baht threshold, the ">=" boundary, and the rule
; that the log never blocks or delays the answer -- is owned here, below. What is still owned
; by nobody is the PERSISTED divergence record, and not by deferral: none of the 89 .sql files
; under migrations/ mentions divergence, so there is no table, column or retention rule for any
; contract to describe, and both emission sites leave a tracing::info! line and nothing else.
; A named refusal below says exactly that, instead of naming a sink that does not exist. And it
; does not carry the Russian wording of the must-say sentence: L3 forbids Cyrillic in a spec,
; so what is pinned is the obligation, not the translation (D13: ru primary, en second).
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module pricing-honesty;

pub const KIND : str = "contract";
pub const ID : str = "turbobaby/pricing-honesty";
pub const NAME : str = "Pricing honesty: an absent rate is not zero";
; Current t27c does not support brace imports. Pricing consumes the boolean result of this
; named contract and deliberately has no offered/stock formula of its own.
pub const REUSES_AVAILABILITY_ID : str = "turbobaby/availability";
pub const DECISIONS : [4]str = ["D9", "D11", "D14", "D15"];
pub const SEED : str = "data/fleet_seed.json";
pub const SEED_MEASURED_AT : str = "2026-09-12";
pub const PRICE_AUTHORITY : str = "door";

; --- what was measured -------------------------------------------------------------------
; Every number below is quoted from data/fleet_seed.json or derived from it in one visible
; step. Nothing is estimated and nothing is carried over from the issue text. Each figure
; carries its provenance on the line ABOVE it, never after the value: a ';' opens a comment
; only at column 1, so an annotation parked at the end of a declaration is not prose to this
; language -- it is a second statement terminator followed by tokens the parser must read as
; code. Provenance that has to compile is provenance that gets deleted.
; Fleet-domain counts belong to canonical availability and are not copied here.
; totals.families_without_published_rate: click-125
pub const FAMILIES_WITHOUT_RATE : u8 = 1;
; Derived: the single rateless family is the one family that is not offered, so no offered
; family is missing a rate. This is the number the issue's "five of thirteen" contradicts.
pub const OFFERED_WITHOUT_RATE : u8 = 0;
; Derived: 13 in-stock rows carrying a rate, plus the 7 price-list-only rows.
pub const PUBLISHED_DAY_RATES : u8 = 20;
; Derived: none of those 20 is 0. The zero case below is therefore hypothetical, not a bike.
pub const ZERO_DAY_RATES : u8 = 0;
; pcx-150, price-list-only: the cheapest number the tariff publishes anywhere.
pub const CHEAPEST_PUBLISHED_DAY_RATE_THB : i16 = 349;
; nmax-155: the cheapest rate attached to a family that actually has units.
; OWNED HERE, and named as owned since 2026-09-24: turbobaby/rental-terms computes its audit
; arithmetic on the same row and carries the figure as REF_BASE_THB_DAY, which it now declares a
; copy of this declaration (REF_BASE_IS_A_COPY, REF_BASE_OWNER_DECLARATION). Gate 3 binds both to
; nmax-155's base_rate_thb_day in data/fleet_seed.json, so neither can move alone.
pub const CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB : i16 = 449;
pub const CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_FAMILY : str = "nmax-155";
pub const CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_RATE_COPY_DECLARATION : str = "REF_BASE_THB_DAY";
; xadv-750: the dearest, and the number that fixes the width of the amount field.
pub const DEAREST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB : i16 = 2788;
; Derived: click-125's rate, deposit and monthly, plus xadv-750's monthly.
pub const NULL_MONEY_FIELDS_IN_STOCK : u8 = 4;
; The issue's figure, kept so that the correction is checkable rather than merely asserted.
pub const ISSUE_CLAIMED_WITHOUT_RATE : u8 = 5;
pub const ISSUE_FIGURE_NOTE : str = "Issue #21 says five of thirteen families have no measured rate. Measured: one of fourteen in-stock, zero of thirteen offered. The seed's totals agree with the measurement.";

; --- the representation ------------------------------------------------------------------
; The discriminant is explicit, and 0 is deliberately NOT a legal constructed tag. D9 records
; three constructs in this tree that turn an unknown number into a confident zero, and one of
; them -- try_get_warn! in src/db/macros.rs -- hands back the typed default on a read error
; with a log line as the only evidence. If RATE_ABSENT were 0, a zero-filled or
; default-initialised record would read as a well-formed measured absence and that bug would
; be invisible. So a record nobody constructed carries tag 0, which is neither absent nor
; present but INVALID; the renderer treats it exactly as it treats absence, and emits no
; number for it either.
pub const RATE_INVALID : u8 = 0;
pub const RATE_ABSENT : u8 = 1;
pub const RATE_PRESENT : u8 = 2;
; The tag set is total: there is no fourth state, and in particular there is no
; "approximately known", no "from", and no "average" state for a rate to hide in.
pub const TAGS : [3]str = ["invalid", "absent", "present"];

; Provenance is part of the value, not caller folklore. Only a number returned by the live door
; may render or enter a cart. A seed/file value is retained for audit comparison only.
pub const SOURCE_NONE : u8 = 0;
pub const SOURCE_DOOR : u8 = 1;
pub const SOURCE_FILE_REFERENCE : u8 = 2;
pub const SOURCE_NAMES : [3]str = ["none", "door", "file_reference"];

; The amount slot of a value that is not present. This is NOT a fallback and NOT a default: a
; fallback is a number substituted for a missing price, and -1 baht per day can never be
; charged, quoted or printed as one. It is a poison marker, chosen so that code reading the
; slot without checking the tag produces something obviously broken instead of something
; plausible -- which is precisely what a 0 in that slot would produce, since D9 measured that
; "a price of 0 reads as FREE". No function here ever renders it as an amount, and that is
; enforced rather than asserted: rate_present below refuses zero and the whole negative half,
; so no value tagged PRESENT can carry either the marker or the D9 "FREE" failure value, and the invariant
; the_reserved_half_is_never_rendered_as_an_amount pins the claim this paragraph makes.
; SHAPE_DASH means the slot was not read.
pub const NOT_AN_AMOUNT_THB_DAY : i16 = -1;

; i16 is wide enough by measurement, not by habit: the dearest published day rate is 2788 and
; the cheapest is 349, so the whole published range sits inside a signed 16-bit field with the
; non-positive half left free for invalid inputs and the poison marker. "Left free" is a claim
; about the constructor and not about the type: the type on its own would let a caller hand 0
; or -1 to rate_present and get a PRESENT value back, so the reservation is kept by the guard.
pub struct OptionalRate {
    tag : u8,
    thb_day : i16,
    source : u8,
}

; --- what a render may emit --------------------------------------------------------------
; Two shapes, and the renderer is total over the tag set: every value maps to one of them.
pub const SHAPE_DASH : u8 = 1;
pub const SHAPE_AMOUNT : u8 = 2;
pub const DASH : str = "-";
pub const UNIT : str = "THB/day";
; An amount is an integer number of baht per day, with no decimal part: all 20 published
; rates in the seed are whole baht. Rounding is not performed here -- it belongs to the
; arithmetic D15 keeps in one place.
pub const AMOUNT_DECIMALS : u8 = 0;

; The obligation that travels with a dash. SAY_HUMAN_QUOTES is what D11's on_silence.must_say
; requires; SAY_NOTHING_EXTRA means the amount speaks for itself.
pub const SAY_NOTHING_EXTRA : u8 = 1;
pub const SAY_HUMAN_QUOTES : u8 = 2;
pub const MUST_SAY : str = "a human quotes this price";
; D11's on_silence.must_not_emit, quoted in the seed's order. Item 5 is the load-bearing one:
; silence is listed alongside invention, so dropping it from this list would turn the dash
; into a licence to say nothing at all.
pub const MUST_NOT_EMIT : [5]str = [
  "an exact number",
  "a 'from' / 'ot' number",
  "an average",
  "a range",
  "silence",
];

; The render result is a typed triple rather than one formatted string, because the typesetting
; is locale work (D13) and this file may hold no Cyrillic (L3). What is pinned is the shape,
; the amount, and the sentence the dash must carry; the locale layer does the wording.
pub struct RenderedRate {
    shape : u8,
    thb_day : i16,
    say : u8,
}

; --- constructors ------------------------------------------------------------------------

; The only door to a PRESENT rate, and it is a guard rather than a wrapper. Zero is the exact
; "FREE" failure value D9 forbids; the negative half is reserved for invalid inputs and the
; poison marker. Both are refused as INVALID instead of being tagged present. This matches the
; shared runtime PRICE boundary in src/trios/pricing.rs and the catalog renderer: finite and strictly
; positive, never merely non-negative (scope clarified 2026-09-22, see the end). i16 already makes NaN and infinity
; unrepresentable, so non-positive values are the remaining unpublishable cases.
; The refused number is not kept in the slot: it is replaced by the marker, because code that
; took the magnitude of a retained -250 would print a plausible 250 THB/day, and -1 is the one
; negative this file has already argued cannot be mistaken for a price.
pub fn rate_present(thb_day: i16) OptionalRate {
    if (thb_day <= 0) {
        return OptionalRate{ .tag = RATE_INVALID, .thb_day = NOT_AN_AMOUNT_THB_DAY, .source = SOURCE_NONE };
    }
    return OptionalRate{ .tag = RATE_PRESENT, .thb_day = thb_day, .source = SOURCE_DOOR };
}

; Positive seed money may be compared with the door for divergence, but is never a client price.
pub fn rate_reference(thb_day: i16) OptionalRate {
    if (thb_day <= 0) {
        return OptionalRate{ .tag = RATE_INVALID, .thb_day = NOT_AN_AMOUNT_THB_DAY, .source = SOURCE_NONE };
    }
    return OptionalRate{ .tag = RATE_PRESENT, .thb_day = thb_day, .source = SOURCE_FILE_REFERENCE };
}

; The only way to say "the source publishes nothing". It takes no amount, because there is no
; amount to take.
pub fn rate_absent() OptionalRate {
    return OptionalRate{ .tag = RATE_ABSENT, .thb_day = NOT_AN_AMOUNT_THB_DAY, .source = SOURCE_NONE };
}

; What a zero-filled or default-initialised record looks like coming out of a fail-open read.
; It is not a value anybody should construct; it exists so the tests can prove that such a
; record does not render as a free bike.
pub fn rate_zero_filled_record() OptionalRate {
    return OptionalRate{ .tag = RATE_INVALID, .thb_day = 0, .source = SOURCE_NONE };
}

pub fn is_present(rate: OptionalRate) bool {
    return rate.tag == RATE_PRESENT;
}

pub fn is_client_price(rate: OptionalRate) bool {
    return is_present(rate) and rate.source == SOURCE_DOOR;
}

; --- the render --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; There is no third branch, because there is no number to put in one. Absent and invalid land
; together: both mean nobody measured a rate, and the client-facing consequence is identical.

pub fn render(rate: OptionalRate) RenderedRate {
    if (is_client_price(rate)) {
        return RenderedRate{ .shape = SHAPE_AMOUNT, .thb_day = rate.thb_day, .say = SAY_NOTHING_EXTRA };
    }
    return RenderedRate{ .shape = SHAPE_DASH, .thb_day = NOT_AN_AMOUNT_THB_DAY, .say = SAY_HUMAN_QUOTES };
}

; --- bookability, which never consults a price -------------------------------------------
; `bookable` is the already-decided boolean supplied by canonical availability. Pricing owns
; only the additional door-provenance gate required before that family may enter a cart.

; D9's fourth construct: 059_cart_tables.sql declares unit_price NOT NULL CHECK (unit_price >= 0),
; so a cart line cannot hold an absence, and the only value that satisfies the column without
; inventing a number is 0 -- which reads as free. The resolution is a refusal, not a zero.
pub fn may_add_to_cart(rate: OptionalRate, bookable: bool) bool {
    if (is_client_price(rate) == false) {
        return false;
    }
    return bookable;
}

; --- D11's divergence decision, and the record nobody owns --------------------------------
; DECISIONS.md:166-167 states the rule in one sentence: "Every priced answer logs any
; divergence of >= 1 baht between door and file, and the logging never blocks or delays the
; answer." Two halves, and the second is the load-bearing one. The first half alone would be
; satisfied by a comparator that refuses the answer when the numbers disagree, which is the
; exact failure D11 forbids at one remove: a client who is told nothing because two internal
; numbers argue has been served silence, and silence is item 5 of MUST_NOT_EMIT.
;
; What is pinned here is the DECISION, not the sink. The threshold, the direction of the
; boundary and the non-blocking rule are all checkable statements about behaviour. Persistence
; is a statement about storage, and the refusal below explains why this file may not make one.

; DECISIONS.md:166. One baht exactly, and the comparison includes the boundary: a gap EQUAL to
; the threshold is reported. src/api/orders.rs:642 writes the same boundary in the runtime as
; (quoted - from_file).abs() >= 1.0, so ">= " here is transcription and not a choice made in
; this file. The unit is baht per day, the same unit as every other amount in this contract.
pub const DIVERGENCE_THRESHOLD_THB_DAY : i16 = 1;

; DECISIONS.md:167, the second half. Both emission sites obey it structurally, not by promise:
; src/api/bikes.rs:649-662 logs inside an if-let and falls through to Ok(value), and
; src/api/orders.rs:845-855 logs inside the loop and falls through to Ok(BikeLineCheck::Ok).
; Neither has a branch that turns a divergence into an error, a retry or a delay.
pub const DIVERGENCE_NEVER_BLOCKS_THE_ANSWER : bool = true;

; Derived in one visible step: the cheapest in-stock rate moved by exactly the threshold. 448
; is no family's tariff anywhere in the seed and is not offered as one -- it is the boundary
; witness, the nearest file-side number that still has to be reported. The derivation is
; asserted below rather than trusted to this comment.
pub const GAP_AT_THRESHOLD_FILE_THB_DAY : i16 = CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB - DIVERGENCE_THRESHOLD_THB_DAY;

; An honest property of the representation, written down because its absence would read as an
; oversight. The runtime compares f64 baht and can therefore see a gap SMALLER than one baht:
; src/api/orders.rs:3732 pins 337.4 against a file-side 337.0, a 0.4 baht gap that is correctly
; not reported. This contract's amounts are whole baht (AMOUNT_DECIMALS is 0), so the smallest
; non-zero gap it can represent IS the threshold, and "below the threshold" here means exactly
; zero. A reader hunting for a sub-baht case in this file would be hunting for something the
; model cannot hold; the runtime test named above is where that case lives.
pub const SUB_BAHT_GAP_IS_UNREPRESENTABLE_HERE : bool = true;

; The file side's number is produced by the class-discount arithmetic, and that arithmetic is
; NOT restated here: src/api/orders.rs:639-641 calls apply_class_discount (src/db/bikes.rs:296)
; then round_half_up_baht (src/db/bikes.rs:312), and the integer statement of that same step
; belongs to the rental-terms contract, whose audit_daily_thb pins 449 at 2500 bp to 337
; (turbobaby/rental-terms owns audit_daily_thb and REF_BASE_THB_DAY; cited by owner ID and
; declaration name rather than by line, because that file is under concurrent edit and a line
; number would rot -- re-opened 2026-09-21, both declarations exist and still carry exactly this
; arithmetic). This file compares two amounts. It
; computes neither of them, and it holds no discount, rate or rounding rule of its own.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-24: "owns REF_BASE_THB_DAY" was half right. Rental-terms owns the arithmetic
; and the choice of NMAX 155 as its reference; the 449 inside REF_BASE_THB_DAY is this file's
; CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB, and rental-terms now declares its constant a copy of that one.
pub const REUSES_RENTAL_TERMS_ID : str = "turbobaby/rental-terms";

; Audit-only, tied to the discriminant instead of repeating the claim. The file side of a
; comparison is exactly a SOURCE_FILE_REFERENCE value, and is_client_price already refuses that
; source, so the file's number has no path to a render. What is NEW is the scope: on the
; divergence path a caller holds both numbers at once for the first time, which is the one
; place where showing "the other one" becomes reachable by accident.
pub const FILE_REFERENCE_IS_AUDIT_ONLY : bool = true;
pub const DIVERGENCE_FILE_SIDE_SOURCE : u8 = SOURCE_FILE_REFERENCE;

; THE REFUSAL (measured 2026-09-20, re-measured 2026-09-21 and unchanged). Persistence is not
; specified here, and not because it was deferred: there is nothing in this repository to
; specify it against. grep -rniE "diverg" over
; migrations/ returns 0 rows. The 90 below is the number of .sql migration files that recursive
; grep actually read: 89 at the top level plus 077_quest_progress.sql in migrations/wip/. It is
; NOT "ls migrations/ | wc -l", which also prints 90 but counts the wip/ DIRECTORY as one of its
; entries and only 89 files -- the right number by the wrong arithmetic, and the two agree here
; by coincidence. (87, 86 and 87 before 087, and 88, 87 and 88 before 088, both 2026-09-24; 89,
; 88 and 89 before 089, 2026-09-26: see the corrections below the count.) So: no table, no column, no id, no retention
; window. Both emission sites are tracing::info!, which is a process log line: it has no schema
; this file could pin, no reader this file could name and no lifetime this file could bound.
; Naming a table, a column set or a retention period would be exactly the invention D11 forbids,
; one level up from the price. When a sink exists, this constant is what has to be deleted.
pub const DIVERGENCE_PERSISTENCE_IS_NOT_SPECIFIED : bool = true;
pub const DIVERGENCE_TABLES : u8 = 0;
; Re-measured 2026-09-26: 90 recursive, 89 at the top level. migrations/089_referral_credit.sql
; arrived (turbobaby/referral-credit, the owner's R3 answer) and creates three tables of its own
; with no divergence sink among them, so the search still finds none. The figures before it are
; kept under _BEFORE_089 names.
pub const MIGRATION_FILES_SEARCHED : u8 = 90;
; THIS CONTRACT OWNS THIS COUNT. turbobaby/locale-policy declares the same figure in a
; declaration of the same name, for a DIFFERENT search over the same directory: it looks for a
; CHECK constraint on a language column where this one looks for a divergence sink. One
; measurement declared twice with no edge between the two files is the drift D15 exists to
; remove. This contract raised the figure first, so the count is owned HERE and carried THERE as
; a named copy that names this ID. Re-measured 2026-09-21 and unchanged at 87: 86 .sql files at
; the top level plus 077_quest_progress.sql in migrations/wip/. The only non-.sql file anywhere
; under migrations/ is migrations/wip/README.md, which is why counting every file returns 88 and
; is the wrong arithmetic for this claim. Re-run the same day, the search for divergence over
; all 87 still returns zero rows, and both emission sites below still read as quoted.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-24: 88, of which 87 at the top level. migrations/087_delivery_zones_phuket.sql
; arrived with the owner's Phuket delivery zones (turbobaby/delivery-terms). The search was re-run
; over all 88 the same day and still returns zero rows for divergence; counting every file under
; migrations/ now returns 89, still the wrong arithmetic for the same reason. The 2026-09-21
; figures are kept below under their own names.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-24, later the same day: 89, of which 88 at the top level.
; migrations/088_unpublish_events.sql arrived with the owner's rental-only ruling
; (turbobaby/events-booking). The divergence search was re-run over all 89 and still returns zero
; rows; counting every file under migrations/ now returns 90. The figures between 087 and 088 are
; kept below under _BEFORE_088 names. The paragraph that follows still reads 88, as written.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-24, the same day: THIS CONTRACT DOES NOT OWN THIS COUNT. The paragraph above claimed it,
; and so did turbobaby/schema-provenance, whose subject is the migration tree: it declares the same
; census as SQL_FILES_RECURSIVE 88, SQL_FILES_TOP_LEVEL 87 and WIP_SQL_FILES 1, names itself the
; census owner, and lists this file as a sibling copy -- while this file never named it. A review of
; 2026-09-23 recorded two self-declared owners of one measurement. Resolved by subject: the census
; is schema-provenance's. What stays here is the USE of the number -- the divergence search read
; all 89 files (90 since 089) and found no sink -- carried as a declared copy with the owner named by ID and by
; declaration, and gate 3 now binds the owner's three figures to the tree beside this file's.
; The claim as written is kept under a _BEFORE_ name, and so is the copy holder it named, because
; turbobaby/locale-policy now names the census owner instead of this file.
pub const MIGRATION_COUNT_IS_OWNED_HERE : bool = false;
pub const MIGRATION_COUNT_IS_OWNED_HERE_BEFORE_2026_09_24 : bool = true;
pub const REUSES_SCHEMA_PROVENANCE_ID : str = "turbobaby/schema-provenance";
pub const MIGRATION_COUNT_OWNER_DECLARATIONS : [3]str = ["SQL_FILES_RECURSIVE", "SQL_FILES_TOP_LEVEL", "WIP_SQL_FILES"];
pub const MIGRATION_COUNT_IS_A_COPY : bool = true;
pub const MIGRATION_COUNT_COPY_HOLDER_ID_BEFORE_2026_09_24 : str = "turbobaby/locale-policy";
pub const MIGRATION_COUNT_TOP_LEVEL : u8 = 89;
pub const MIGRATION_FILES_SEARCHED_BEFORE_089 : u8 = 89;
pub const MIGRATION_COUNT_TOP_LEVEL_BEFORE_089 : u8 = 88;
pub const MIGRATION_COUNT_IN_WIP : u8 = 1;
pub const MIGRATION_COUNT_REMEASURED_AT : str = "2026-09-24";
pub const MIGRATION_COUNT_OWNERSHIP_RESOLVED_AT : str = "2026-09-24";
pub const MIGRATION_FILES_SEARCHED_BEFORE_087 : u8 = 87;
pub const MIGRATION_COUNT_TOP_LEVEL_BEFORE_087 : u8 = 86;
pub const MIGRATION_COUNT_REMEASURED_AT_BEFORE_087 : str = "2026-09-21";
pub const MIGRATION_FILES_SEARCHED_BEFORE_088 : u8 = 88;
pub const MIGRATION_COUNT_TOP_LEVEL_BEFORE_088 : u8 = 87;
pub const DIVERGENCE_SINK_KIND : str = "process log line";
pub const DIVERGENCE_SINKS : [2]str = [
  "src/api/bikes.rs:655-660",
  "src/api/orders.rs:848-853",
];
pub const DIVERGENCE_PERSISTENCE_NOTE : str = "No sink exists: none of the 90 .sql migration files under migrations/ (89 at the top level plus one in migrations/wip/) mentions divergence, so there is no table, column or retention rule to pin. The only trace either priced answer leaves is a tracing::info! line at src/api/bikes.rs:655-660 and src/api/orders.rs:848-853. The decision is owned here; the record is owned by nobody.";

; The file side of a comparison, as a predicate. is_client_price already names the door side;
; this is its counterpart, and it exists so that divergence_report_required can refuse a
; mislabelled pair instead of comparing a door number against another door number.
pub fn is_file_reference(rate: OptionalRate) bool {
    return is_present(rate) and rate.source == SOURCE_FILE_REFERENCE;
}

; Unsigned distance between two amounts, in whole baht. Both published bounds fit in i16 and so
; does their widest possible difference (2788 - 349), so no comparison here can overflow.
pub fn amount_gap_thb_day(a: i16, b: i16) i16 {
    if (a >= b) {
        return a - b;
    }
    return b - a;
}

; Whether D11 requires a report. Three refusals before the arithmetic, and each mirrors a
; branch of src/api/orders.rs:634-647: no door number means no priced answer to log against
; (the runtime's quoted filter at :640), no file number means nothing to compare (the runtime's
; ? at :641), and only then is the gap measured against the threshold. A mislabelled pair --
; two door values, or a reference value passed as the door -- is refused rather than compared,
; because a divergence between a number and itself is not evidence of anything.
pub fn divergence_report_required(door: OptionalRate, file_ref: OptionalRate) bool {
    if (is_client_price(door) == false) {
        return false;
    }
    if (is_file_reference(file_ref) == false) {
        return false;
    }
    return amount_gap_thb_day(door.thb_day, file_ref.thb_day) >= DIVERGENCE_THRESHOLD_THB_DAY;
}

; The non-blocking half, written as code so that it can be checked rather than believed. The
; branch is real and both arms are deliberately identical: whatever the comparison decides, the
; customer is handed render(door) and nothing else. The file side never reaches this return
; value, and there is no third arm in which a divergence withholds the answer.
pub fn answer_despite_divergence(door: OptionalRate, file_ref: OptionalRate) RenderedRate {
    if (divergence_report_required(door, file_ref)) {
        return render(door);
    }
    return render(door);
}

; --- tests -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

test the_absent_case_renders_a_dash_and_the_sentence {
    assert is_present(rate_absent()) == false;
    assert render(rate_absent()).shape == SHAPE_DASH;
    assert render(rate_absent()).say == SAY_HUMAN_QUOTES;
    assert render(rate_absent()).thb_day != 0;
}

; Zero is the D9 regression case. No family in the corpus is free: of the 20 published day
; rates the smallest is 349 baht, and ZERO_DAY_RATES is 0. The constructor must therefore
; reject zero before either the amount renderer or the cart sees it.
test the_zero_case_is_invalid_and_renders_the_honest_fallback {
    assert ZERO_DAY_RATES == 0;
    assert rate_present(0).tag == RATE_INVALID;
    assert is_present(rate_present(0)) == false;
    assert render(rate_present(0)).shape == SHAPE_DASH;
    assert render(rate_present(0)).thb_day == NOT_AN_AMOUNT_THB_DAY;
    assert render(rate_present(0)).say == SAY_HUMAN_QUOTES;
    assert may_add_to_cart(rate_present(0), true) == false;
}

; The reserved half, as a case. Zero and negatives are equally unpublishable, but for different
; reasons: zero reads as FREE while a negative is not money. -1 is the marker itself; -250 is
; the dangerous shape, a plausible magnitude wearing a minus sign. Both are refused at the
; constructor, so neither reaches a render as an amount and neither reaches a cart.
test a_negative_amount_is_invalid_not_a_price {
    assert is_present(rate_present(NOT_AN_AMOUNT_THB_DAY)) == false;
    assert rate_present(NOT_AN_AMOUNT_THB_DAY).tag == RATE_INVALID;
    assert rate_present(-250).thb_day == NOT_AN_AMOUNT_THB_DAY;
    assert render(rate_present(-250)).shape == SHAPE_DASH;
    assert render(rate_present(-250)).say == SAY_HUMAN_QUOTES;
    assert may_add_to_cart(rate_present(-250), true) == false;
}

; The measured bounds exercise the amount width. rate_present represents the door returning the
; number; rate_reference below represents that same number read from the seed.
test the_normal_case_renders_the_number_it_was_given {
    assert render(rate_present(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB)).shape == SHAPE_AMOUNT;
    assert render(rate_present(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB)).thb_day == 449;
    assert render(rate_present(DEAREST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB)).thb_day == 2788;
}

test a_file_reference_is_audit_evidence_not_a_client_price {
    assert is_present(rate_reference(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB)) == true;
    assert is_client_price(rate_reference(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB)) == false;
    assert render(rate_reference(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB)).shape == SHAPE_DASH;
    assert may_add_to_cart(rate_reference(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB), true) == false;
    assert rate_present(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB).source == SOURCE_DOOR;
}

; Absence and an invalid zero remain distinct source states, but their customer-facing result is
; deliberately identical: no amount, plus the human-quote obligation.
test absent_and_zero_have_distinct_tags_but_the_same_safe_render {
    assert render(rate_absent()).shape == render(rate_present(0)).shape;
    assert render(rate_absent()).thb_day == render(rate_present(0)).thb_day;
    assert render(rate_absent()).say == render(rate_present(0)).say;
    assert rate_absent().tag != rate_present(0).tag;
}

; The D9 defect, stated as a case: a fail-open read yields a zero-filled record, and a
; zero-filled record must not become a free bike.
test a_zero_filled_record_does_not_render_as_free {
    assert render(rate_zero_filled_record()).shape == SHAPE_DASH;
    assert render(rate_zero_filled_record()).say == SAY_HUMAN_QUOTES;
    assert render(rate_zero_filled_record()).thb_day != 0;
    assert is_present(rate_zero_filled_record()) == false;
}

test an_absent_rate_is_never_addable_to_a_cart {
    assert may_add_to_cart(rate_absent(), true) == false;
    assert may_add_to_cart(rate_zero_filled_record(), true) == false;
    assert may_add_to_cart(rate_present(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB), true) == true;
}

; The measured absence: one family, not five. click-125 fails bookability twice over --
; offered:false and 0 of 1 units available -- so the rateless family is also the unbookable one.
test the_measured_absence_is_one_family_not_five {
    assert FAMILIES_WITHOUT_RATE == 1;
    assert OFFERED_WITHOUT_RATE == 0;
    assert ISSUE_CLAIMED_WITHOUT_RATE != FAMILIES_WITHOUT_RATE;
}

; The mirror absence, and the larger one: 7 families carry a published rate and no stock. A
; rate is not stock, so pricing one of them is still not an offer to rent it.
test a_published_rate_with_a_false_bookability_input_cannot_enter_a_cart {
    assert may_add_to_cart(rate_present(CHEAPEST_PUBLISHED_DAY_RATE_THB), false) == false;
}

; Bookability is a fleet fact, so the price never reaches this decision. forza-300 and
; mt-03-300 are the live case: both offered, both priced, both at 0 units available.
test pricing_consumes_bookability_without_reimplementing_availability {
    assert REUSES_AVAILABILITY_ID == "turbobaby/availability";
    assert may_add_to_cart(rate_present(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB), false) == false;
    assert may_add_to_cart(rate_present(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB), true) == true;
}

test the_published_rates_are_counted_and_none_is_free {
    assert PUBLISHED_DAY_RATES == 20;
    assert CHEAPEST_PUBLISHED_DAY_RATE_THB == 349;
    assert CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB == 449;
    assert DEAREST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB == 2788;
    assert NULL_MONEY_FIELDS_IN_STOCK == 4;
}

; ---- D11's divergence boundary ----------------------------------------------------------
; The door quotes the cheapest in-stock rate, 449. The file side is that same number, then that
; same number moved by exactly the threshold. Equality and the boundary are the two cases the
; ">=" in DECISIONS.md:166 actually distinguishes, so they are the two cases pinned.
test the_divergence_report_boundary_sits_exactly_at_one_baht {
    assert DIVERGENCE_THRESHOLD_THB_DAY == 1;
    assert GAP_AT_THRESHOLD_FILE_THB_DAY == CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB - DIVERGENCE_THRESHOLD_THB_DAY;
    assert amount_gap_thb_day(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB, CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB) == 0;
    assert divergence_report_required(rate_present(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB), rate_reference(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB)) == false;
    assert amount_gap_thb_day(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB, GAP_AT_THRESHOLD_FILE_THB_DAY) == DIVERGENCE_THRESHOLD_THB_DAY;
    assert divergence_report_required(rate_present(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB), rate_reference(GAP_AT_THRESHOLD_FILE_THB_DAY)) == true;
}

; "Below the threshold" is not a second case in this model, it is the same case, and saying so
; out loud is the point of this test. In whole baht the only gap smaller than one baht is zero,
; so equality IS the sub-threshold case here; the fractional one the runtime can see is pinned
; in Rust at src/api/orders.rs:3732 and cannot be written down in an integer contract.
test below_the_threshold_means_exactly_zero_in_whole_baht {
    assert SUB_BAHT_GAP_IS_UNREPRESENTABLE_HERE == true;
    assert AMOUNT_DECIMALS == 0;
    assert amount_gap_thb_day(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB, CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB) < DIVERGENCE_THRESHOLD_THB_DAY;
    assert divergence_report_required(rate_present(DEAREST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB), rate_reference(DEAREST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB)) == false;
}

; The widest gap this file's own measured bounds can produce, 2788 against 349. It is here to
; catch an implementation that reports only an exact one-baht difference instead of everything
; at or above it, and to show the comparison is symmetric in its two arguments.
test a_gap_far_above_the_threshold_is_reported_in_either_direction {
    assert amount_gap_thb_day(DEAREST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB, CHEAPEST_PUBLISHED_DAY_RATE_THB) == 2439;
    assert amount_gap_thb_day(CHEAPEST_PUBLISHED_DAY_RATE_THB, DEAREST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB) == 2439;
    assert divergence_report_required(rate_present(DEAREST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB), rate_reference(CHEAPEST_PUBLISHED_DAY_RATE_THB)) == true;
    assert divergence_report_required(rate_present(CHEAPEST_PUBLISHED_DAY_RATE_THB), rate_reference(DEAREST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB)) == true;
}

; The non-blocking half of DECISIONS.md:166-167, as the three cases side by side. Agreement, a
; divergence exactly at the boundary, and a divergence far past it all hand the customer the
; identical triple: the amount shape, the door's own 449, and no extra sentence.
test the_customer_is_told_the_same_thing_in_every_divergence_case {
    assert answer_despite_divergence(rate_present(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB), rate_reference(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB)).shape == SHAPE_AMOUNT;
    assert answer_despite_divergence(rate_present(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB), rate_reference(GAP_AT_THRESHOLD_FILE_THB_DAY)).shape == SHAPE_AMOUNT;
    assert answer_despite_divergence(rate_present(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB), rate_reference(DEAREST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB)).shape == SHAPE_AMOUNT;
    assert answer_despite_divergence(rate_present(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB), rate_reference(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB)).thb_day == CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB;
    assert answer_despite_divergence(rate_present(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB), rate_reference(GAP_AT_THRESHOLD_FILE_THB_DAY)).thb_day == CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB;
    assert answer_despite_divergence(rate_present(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB), rate_reference(DEAREST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB)).thb_day == CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB;
    assert answer_despite_divergence(rate_present(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB), rate_reference(GAP_AT_THRESHOLD_FILE_THB_DAY)).say == SAY_NOTHING_EXTRA;
    assert DIVERGENCE_NEVER_BLOCKS_THE_ANSWER == true;
}

; The audit-only rule at the one place it becomes reachable: the caller is holding both numbers.
; 448 is the file's number in the boundary case above, and it is exactly what the answer must
; NOT contain. A source-tagged pair is also checked for mislabelling in both directions.
test the_file_side_of_a_divergence_is_never_shown_to_a_client {
    assert FILE_REFERENCE_IS_AUDIT_ONLY == true;
    assert DIVERGENCE_FILE_SIDE_SOURCE == SOURCE_FILE_REFERENCE;
    assert is_file_reference(rate_reference(GAP_AT_THRESHOLD_FILE_THB_DAY)) == true;
    assert is_file_reference(rate_present(GAP_AT_THRESHOLD_FILE_THB_DAY)) == false;
    assert is_client_price(rate_reference(GAP_AT_THRESHOLD_FILE_THB_DAY)) == false;
    assert render(rate_reference(GAP_AT_THRESHOLD_FILE_THB_DAY)).shape == SHAPE_DASH;
    assert answer_despite_divergence(rate_present(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB), rate_reference(GAP_AT_THRESHOLD_FILE_THB_DAY)).thb_day != GAP_AT_THRESHOLD_FILE_THB_DAY;
}

; A silent door is the absence path, not a divergence with one side missing. The runtime agrees
; by construction -- src/api/orders.rs:640 drops out before the comparison -- and the customer
; gets the dash and the sentence, never a comparison against the file's number. The mirror case
; is here too: a missing file side is nothing to compare, not a divergence of the whole amount.
test an_absent_door_amount_is_the_absence_path_and_never_a_divergence {
    assert divergence_report_required(rate_absent(), rate_reference(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB)) == false;
    assert divergence_report_required(rate_zero_filled_record(), rate_reference(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB)) == false;
    assert divergence_report_required(rate_present(0), rate_reference(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB)) == false;
    assert divergence_report_required(rate_present(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB), rate_absent()) == false;
    assert answer_despite_divergence(rate_absent(), rate_reference(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB)).shape == SHAPE_DASH;
    assert answer_despite_divergence(rate_absent(), rate_reference(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB)).say == SAY_HUMAN_QUOTES;
    assert answer_despite_divergence(rate_absent(), rate_reference(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB)).thb_day == NOT_AN_AMOUNT_THB_DAY;
}

; The refusal, as a case rather than as a paragraph. If a migration ever creates a divergence
; table, DIVERGENCE_TABLES stops being 0 and this test is the first thing that has to change.
test persistence_of_a_divergence_is_refused_for_lack_of_a_sink {
    assert DIVERGENCE_PERSISTENCE_IS_NOT_SPECIFIED == true;
    assert DIVERGENCE_TABLES == 0;
    assert MIGRATION_FILES_SEARCHED == 90;
    assert DIVERGENCE_SINK_KIND == "process log line";
    assert DIVERGENCE_SINKS.len == 2;
    assert DIVERGENCE_SINKS[0] == "src/api/bikes.rs:655-660";
    assert DIVERGENCE_SINKS[1] == "src/api/orders.rs:848-853";
}

; The file side's number is somebody else's output. Naming that owner is what keeps this
; contract from growing a second copy of the class-discount step.
; The count this contract USES, and whose it is. Until 2026-09-24 this test was named for owning
; the count and naming its copy holder; the census is turbobaby/schema-provenance's, and the test
; now says so. It still fails the day the two halves of the directory stop adding up to the whole,
; which is the arithmetic that made the wrong version of this measurement look right.
test the_migration_file_count_is_a_named_copy_of_the_schema_census {
  assert MIGRATION_FILES_SEARCHED == 90;
  assert MIGRATION_COUNT_IS_OWNED_HERE == false;
  assert MIGRATION_COUNT_IS_OWNED_HERE_BEFORE_2026_09_24 == true;
  assert MIGRATION_COUNT_IS_A_COPY == true;
  assert REUSES_SCHEMA_PROVENANCE_ID == "turbobaby/schema-provenance";
  assert REUSES_SCHEMA_PROVENANCE_ID != ID;
  assert MIGRATION_COUNT_OWNER_DECLARATIONS.len == 3;
  assert MIGRATION_COUNT_OWNER_DECLARATIONS[0] == "SQL_FILES_RECURSIVE";
  assert MIGRATION_COUNT_OWNER_DECLARATIONS[1] == "SQL_FILES_TOP_LEVEL";
  assert MIGRATION_COUNT_OWNER_DECLARATIONS[2] == "WIP_SQL_FILES";
  assert MIGRATION_COUNT_OWNERSHIP_RESOLVED_AT == "2026-09-24";
  assert MIGRATION_COUNT_TOP_LEVEL == 89;
  assert MIGRATION_FILES_SEARCHED == MIGRATION_FILES_SEARCHED_BEFORE_089 + 1;
  assert MIGRATION_COUNT_TOP_LEVEL_BEFORE_089 + MIGRATION_COUNT_IN_WIP == MIGRATION_FILES_SEARCHED_BEFORE_089;
  assert MIGRATION_COUNT_IN_WIP == 1;
  assert MIGRATION_COUNT_TOP_LEVEL + MIGRATION_COUNT_IN_WIP == MIGRATION_FILES_SEARCHED;
  assert MIGRATION_COUNT_COPY_HOLDER_ID_BEFORE_2026_09_24 == "turbobaby/locale-policy";
  assert MIGRATION_COUNT_COPY_HOLDER_ID_BEFORE_2026_09_24 != ID;
  assert MIGRATION_COUNT_REMEASURED_AT == "2026-09-24";
  assert MIGRATION_FILES_SEARCHED_BEFORE_087 == 87;
  assert MIGRATION_COUNT_TOP_LEVEL_BEFORE_087 + MIGRATION_COUNT_IN_WIP == MIGRATION_FILES_SEARCHED_BEFORE_087;
  assert MIGRATION_FILES_SEARCHED_BEFORE_089 == MIGRATION_FILES_SEARCHED_BEFORE_088 + 1;
  assert MIGRATION_FILES_SEARCHED_BEFORE_088 == MIGRATION_FILES_SEARCHED_BEFORE_087 + 1;
  assert MIGRATION_COUNT_TOP_LEVEL_BEFORE_088 + MIGRATION_COUNT_IN_WIP == MIGRATION_FILES_SEARCHED_BEFORE_088;
  assert MIGRATION_COUNT_REMEASURED_AT_BEFORE_087 == "2026-09-21";
  assert DIVERGENCE_TABLES == 0;
}

test the_file_side_arithmetic_is_owned_by_the_rental_terms_contract {
    assert REUSES_RENTAL_TERMS_ID == "turbobaby/rental-terms";
    assert REUSES_RENTAL_TERMS_ID != ID;
    assert REUSES_RENTAL_TERMS_ID != REUSES_AVAILABILITY_ID;
    assert CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_FAMILY == "nmax-155";
    assert CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_RATE_COPY_DECLARATION == "REF_BASE_THB_DAY";
}

; --- invariants --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Claims about the whole module that no single example carries.

; The acceptance criterion, as a property: absence has no path to a number at all, so it can
; never arrive at zero. Nothing in this file maps an absence to an amount.
invariant absent_never_maps_to_zero
    assert render(rate_absent()).thb_day != 0 and render(rate_absent()).shape != SHAPE_AMOUNT

; D9 at the constructor boundary: a literal zero can never acquire the PRESENT tag or enter a cart.
invariant zero_never_maps_to_present
    assert is_present(rate_present(0)) == false and may_add_to_cart(rate_present(0), true) == false

; The other acceptance criterion. Bookability is decided without a price, so the implication
; is a real claim and not a definition: a family with no rate cannot be transacted, whatever
; the fleet says about its stock.
invariant bookable_implies_present
    assert may_add_to_cart(rate_absent(), true) == false and may_add_to_cart(rate_zero_filled_record(), true) == false

; And the same claim about the corpus rather than about the code: no offered family in the
; seed lacks a rate, so no bookable family does either.
invariant every_bookable_family_in_the_seed_has_a_rate
    assert OFFERED_WITHOUT_RATE == 0

invariant absent_and_present_are_distinct_tags
    assert RATE_ABSENT != RATE_PRESENT

invariant only_the_door_can_produce_a_client_price
    assert is_client_price(rate_present(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB)) == true and is_client_price(rate_reference(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB)) == false

; A zero-filled record is invalid, not absent. This is what keeps a fail-open read from
; passing as a measurement.
invariant a_zero_filled_record_is_not_a_measured_absence
    assert RATE_ABSENT != RATE_INVALID and RATE_PRESENT != RATE_INVALID

invariant the_tag_set_is_total
    assert TAGS.len == 3

; The dash and the amount are different shapes, which is the whole reason the render returns a
; discriminant instead of a string.
invariant a_dash_is_not_an_amount
    assert SHAPE_DASH != SHAPE_AMOUNT

; Silence is the other half of the offence, so the dash is never emitted on its own.
invariant the_dash_never_travels_alone
    assert render(rate_absent()).say == SAY_HUMAN_QUOTES and SAY_HUMAN_QUOTES != SAY_NOTHING_EXTRA

; The poison marker is not a price: negative, non-zero, and below every published rate, the
; cheapest of which is pcx-150's 349. The third conjunct is what makes the third adjective
; true, and it is the one that would fail first if the marker were ever moved into range.
invariant the_absent_slot_holds_nothing_publishable
    assert NOT_AN_AMOUNT_THB_DAY < 0 and NOT_AN_AMOUNT_THB_DAY != 0 and NOT_AN_AMOUNT_THB_DAY < CHEAPEST_PUBLISHED_DAY_RATE_THB

; And the marker is reserved in fact, not only in prose: handed to the one constructor that
; can produce a PRESENT value, it comes back as a dash carrying the sentence. Without this
; the paragraph above NOT_AN_AMOUNT_THB_DAY would be a promise no test collects on, and
; "-1 THB/day" would be a legal render.
invariant the_reserved_half_is_never_rendered_as_an_amount
    assert render(rate_present(NOT_AN_AMOUNT_THB_DAY)).shape == SHAPE_DASH and render(rate_present(NOT_AN_AMOUNT_THB_DAY)).say == SAY_HUMAN_QUOTES

; Five prohibitions, and the fifth is silence. A deletion from this list would license the
; failure this spec exists to forbid, so the length is load-bearing.
invariant the_prohibited_emissions_are_whole
    assert MUST_NOT_EMIT.len == 5

; The issue's premise, refuted in the file that closes it.
invariant the_issue_figure_was_not_reproducible
    assert ISSUE_CLAIMED_WITHOUT_RATE != FAMILIES_WITHOUT_RATE and FAMILIES_WITHOUT_RATE == 1

; The claim D11's second half is really making, as a property rather than as an example. The
; first conjunct is what gives the second one its force: the two inputs genuinely disagree
; about whether a report is owed -- one true, one false -- and the customer's amount is the
; same number in both. Without the first conjunct this would hold vacuously for two identical
; inputs and would prove nothing at all.
invariant a_reported_divergence_and_a_silent_one_produce_the_same_answer
    assert divergence_report_required(rate_present(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB), rate_reference(GAP_AT_THRESHOLD_FILE_THB_DAY)) != divergence_report_required(rate_present(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB), rate_reference(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB)) and answer_despite_divergence(rate_present(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB), rate_reference(GAP_AT_THRESHOLD_FILE_THB_DAY)).thb_day == answer_despite_divergence(rate_present(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB), rate_reference(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB)).thb_day

; All three fields of the answer, so that "the same answer" means the whole triple and not just
; the number: a divergence may not silently swap the shape or attach the human-quote sentence
; to a perfectly good amount either. Silence is item 5 of MUST_NOT_EMIT, and a divergence that
; downgraded a priced answer to a dash would be committing it.
invariant no_divergence_outcome_changes_the_shape_the_amount_or_the_sentence
    assert answer_despite_divergence(rate_present(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB), rate_reference(GAP_AT_THRESHOLD_FILE_THB_DAY)).shape == SHAPE_AMOUNT and answer_despite_divergence(rate_present(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB), rate_reference(GAP_AT_THRESHOLD_FILE_THB_DAY)).say == SAY_NOTHING_EXTRA and answer_despite_divergence(rate_present(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB), rate_reference(GAP_AT_THRESHOLD_FILE_THB_DAY)).thb_day != GAP_AT_THRESHOLD_FILE_THB_DAY

; The threshold is a positive whole baht, and the boundary witness is derived from it rather
; than typed in. If either number is edited alone, this fails.
invariant the_divergence_threshold_is_one_whole_baht
    assert DIVERGENCE_THRESHOLD_THB_DAY == 1 and DIVERGENCE_THRESHOLD_THB_DAY > 0 and GAP_AT_THRESHOLD_FILE_THB_DAY == CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB - DIVERGENCE_THRESHOLD_THB_DAY

; D11's two halves must not be allowed to swap places: a silent door produces the dash and the
; sentence, and never a comparison, so no divergence path can be reached from an absence.
invariant a_silent_door_is_an_absence_and_never_a_divergence
    assert divergence_report_required(rate_absent(), rate_reference(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB)) == false and answer_despite_divergence(rate_absent(), rate_reference(CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB)).say == SAY_HUMAN_QUOTES

; Refused for cause, not deferred to later. The cause is a measurement -- zero divergence tables
; in 88 migrations, two tracing sites -- so the refusal expires the day that measurement changes.
invariant the_persisted_divergence_record_is_refused_not_deferred
    assert DIVERGENCE_PERSISTENCE_IS_NOT_SPECIFIED == true and DIVERGENCE_TABLES == 0 and DIVERGENCE_SINKS.len == 2

; CLARIFIED 2026-09-22, by the order-presentation money repair (turbobaby/order-presentation). The
; constructors section calls the shared runtime boundary in src/trios/pricing.rs finite and
; strictly positive, never merely non-negative. That sentence is about the PRICE boundary,
; published_money, and it still holds. Since that day the same module also holds measured_money, a
; separate boundary for the figures a stored ORDER carries -- a bonus of none, no stars spent, a
; total the discounts paid in full -- where zero is a measurement and not an unpublished price.
; published_money is written on top of it (the order filter plus the refusal of zero), so unusable
; money is still defined once. Nothing this file owns changes: it governs one value, the per-day
; rate of a bike family, and an order figure is not that value. The sentence its SHAPE_DASH carries
; is not claimed by the order screens either; that contract records the absence as an open owner
; question.
